  "problem": "An explicit without-Census filter could fail to exclude Census sources, or could exclude unrelated records that merely mention the word census. Maternal mortality could promote infant mortality as the leading compatible result. Title-only answers could be treated as scientific matches. PSI could stand in for readmissions, quality stars for provider relief, and enforcement actions for rate filings. A later observation year could silently satisfy a requested year. The nonsense-plus-Pennsylvania query could return geography-only hits. Held-out labels could leak into ranking. Editing fingerprint-sealed question-parser.mjs or retrieval-core-v1.2.mjs would break retrieval algorithm fingerprints and subject-shortcircuit byte-parity.",
  "resulting_behavior": "Relevance policy lives in packages/enrichment/relevance.mjs with fixtures under evaluation/research-program/relevance/. Near-miss fixtures identify forbidden, uncertain and contextual matches; no test expects a title-only answer. An explicit without-Census filter excludes Census by source identity, not the word census in unrelated prose. Maternal mortality does not promote infant data as the leading compatible result. Ranking reasons agree with actual filters. The nonsense-plus-Pennsylvania query remains a scoped zero. Held-out reviewer labels are unused. Fingerprint-sealed packages/retrieval/tools/question-parser.mjs (10068 bytes), retrieval-core-v1.2.mjs (48161 bytes) and controlled-vocabulary.json (11268 bytes) are unchanged.",
